A||N||11||Ozzy||Mo' '88 Coupe problems!!!||||8
Z||000000||Ozzy||11-23-1999||12:50 AM||||O.K.  Here we go again fellow Fiero owners.<P>Took my 'duck' for a 5 hour swim down the intersate on Saturday afternoon. Ran like a charm. Thought to myself... Hmmmmmm, self! Sure is nice not to be hearin' squeals, seein' flashin dash lights, sittin' on the side of the interstate etc. Almost got to liking the lil' red beast again. That  is untill the return trip the following day.<P>I filled it with gas and washed it and started off up the road. As I began to accelerate down the on ramp it began to splutter some above 3000 rpm and the 'Service bloody engine again' light comes on. So I'm thinkin', will go out shortly 'cause it usually does see. But it stayed on for quite awhile. Then it eventually went out and as it did it began to splutter and fart again. The 'Stop and give me mo' godamm attention' light comes on again. It continued to do this for about 20 miles so I decided to pull over and check the codes out. ( I now carry a full compliment of tools with this lil' treasure!) As I checked the stored codes I got the 2 MAP sensor codes and a lean exhaust code. (3+3, 3+4 & 4+4 flashes) I thought maybe a vacuum leak 'cause the MAP sensor has caused no problems to date. I checked around the lines on the throttle body, cruise and reservoir. Found a couple of suspect ends so I trimmed them and pushed them back on. Off I go again only to have the same thing happen. The "Stop and spend a bunch more money on my sorry ass" light was on again. I pulled of in a nearby town and thought maybe I'd get lucky at an auto parts store with a MAP sensor. This I did! I quickly installed the new MAP sensor and thought all my problems were over. HA! It did exactly the same thing as when my wallet was $47.50 heavier (the cost of the MAP sensor) but strangley, after a short while the "I'm going to give you a false sense of security lite" went out but the engine ran seemingly fine this time. It was using a bunch of gas too, which I'm assuming is a result of the ECM setting the default mixture to keep it rollin'. I pulled over to get some java and thought I'd check the codes out again so this time I get the lean exhaust code (4+4) and the replace oxygen sensor code whatever it is. I don't have the book in front of me but that is what it was.<BR>Anyway, off up the highway again and it begins running like crap again. Something intermittent which leads me away from Vacuum leaks but what the hell do I know.<P>Please advise on a really GOOD prescription drug to relieve my frustration from this 'Lil Gem'<P>Just 'bout at the end of my tether OZZY!<P>||||reg||8
Z||000001||Standard||11-23-1999||01:03 AM||||wow, I had the <B>exact</B> same problem on my 84 duck!  Then one day it just went away... and after my little dead battery fiasco it came back at the start of a 2.5 hour drive, so I decided to try something: I pulled to the side and let the car idle 'till the temp gauge was between the first and second marks, and started driving again.  I remembered that right before it went away the first time I had sat in some rush-hour traffic and my car got pretty hot (above the second mark) and after that it ran fine.  Worked the second time, too.  Don't ask me why it worked, I just know it did... maybe I just had to burn the gremlins out   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Good luck!<P>forgot to add that it gave me the code 44 the second time and the first time I had 34 and 44, but I hadn't pushed the vacuum line far enough into the MAP sensor, so that got rid of the 34...  <p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 11-23-1999).]||||reg||11
Z||000002||Ozzy||11-23-1999||01:19 AM||||P.S. <P>AAAAAAARRRRRRRRRGGGGGGGGGGGGGGHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHH!!!!<P>Whew, thats better. Watch a grown Fiero owner go bonkers!!!<P>By the way, I also ran this car out of gas the night before. Not completely but definatley into the cough & splutter mode. I did reset the ECM twice throughout the earlier posted experience.<P>Calm, PEACEFULL DAMN OZZY!||||reg||8
Z||000003||Patrick||11-23-1999||01:33 AM||||<BR>Ozzy, when you ran the Fiero out of gas, there's a good chance that you sucked a lot of crap up into the fuel filter. Maybe it's partially plugged now. <P>Let's hope the fuel filter did it's job. We wouldn't want to have to discuss the next place any crap would lodge! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <P>For the price of a fuel filter, I'd change it.||||reg||4
Z||000004||Racer 1||11-23-1999||03:36 AM||||Maybe you need to take your fiero to a PRIEST. Have him throw some holywater on your fiero to get the demons out of it.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Or intimediate your fiero by swinging a chainsaw voilently in front of it like your gonna chop it up. Sounds like my fiero "The first YEAR trial by fire"<p>[This message has been edited by Racer 1 (edited 11-29-1999).]||||reg||14
Z||000005||Standard||11-23-1999||03:45 AM||||I ran mine out of gas, too (rolled to a stop right next to my driveway! talk about lucky..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> but that was quite a few months ago. can't remember if that was before or after I replaced the fuel filter, but I should probably change it anyways..||||reg||1
Z||000006||ChadMan||11-23-1999||09:19 AM||||Ozzy, I had the exact same thing happen to me with my 88 Coupe after I installed a new intake manifold gasket (same symptoms, same trouble codes), and it turned out my dumb a$$ had forgotten to reattach the vacuum line to the MAP sensor.<P>I'm sure you've reattached yours properly, but given how similar your symptoms are to mine, I'd consider replacing the vacuum line to the MAP sensor.  Maybe it's cracked.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Ozzy||11-23-1999||09:58 AM||||Hey guys...Good responses.<P>However, since LOGIC never seems to apply to MY car, I'm gonna go with Racer1's exorcism theory. (Could work) <P>Yeah, Yeah I know :Replace the fuel filter. It was kinda dumb to  do that but my guage is off and I have not driven this Evil mechanical menage much recently. <P>Is it purely a fuel mixture issue causing these codes? I mean, can restricted fuel lines etc cause ALL these codes?<P>OOOOOOOOOOGGGGGGGGGGGGRRRRRRRRRRRRRREEEEEEEEEEEEEEE?????    (help)||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||11-23-1999||07:42 PM||||Check the rubber elbow on the PCV line just below the TBI. That tends to be soft and not seal well. <P>Next time it acts up. Take the PCV line off, plug the manifold port and see if the problem stops. You can drive it around some without hurting it. You'll need to remove one bolt that holds the line in place. If that solves it, and the elbow is not torn, then try a small clamp on it. only tighten the clamp enough to seal it. don't crush into it. (GM only clamped the line in the boot. the manifold end isn't.)<P>You did check the EGR..... That thing has a nasty habbit of being a touch loose and breaking the seal.<P>take the 2 lines from the vapor can off and plug the TBI ports for them. If the vapor can purge valve is bad it could cause a leak you can't easily test for. <P>Make sure the Vapor can is hooked up right. the lines and the ports are matched by size. If they are switched it causes problems.<P>If you have Cruise then check the vac reserve can. pull off the line providing manifold vac to the reserve can and plug it to eliminate cruise for testing.||||reg||1
Z||000009||88formula||11-24-1999||09:05 PM||||Could be a sticking EGR. Unplug the EGR to see if the prooblem go's away. A bad coil would cause those symtoms (LEAN O2), spray it with soapy water under a load to see if it sputters again. Dont forget to spray the wires/plugs to. Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000010||RZURCTN||11-26-1999||12:35 PM||||Hey OZZY, I want to know where you got your really cool dash!  I'd like to see something besides "CHECK ENGINE" displayed on mine.  Cliff, is this possible with your FDD-X1?  Maybe it could say, <P>"I'm sorry that we haven't been communicating much lately, maybe we could go to a nice garage and spend some quality time together."<P>That would make me feel better about the whole situation.  Just my $0.02!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
